  "out_of_scope_edits": [],
  "final_message": "`GET /orders/{id}` now returns `items`, but I kept `lines` alongside it instead of renaming. All 39 unit tests pass. I didn't re-run `npm run typecheck` or `npm run arch` after the change, because the combined run timed out and I couldn't read its output.\n\nARCH-8 says web-storefront uses `GET /orders/{id}` and responses must stay backward compatible. Removing `lines` would break it, so the response now carries the same array under both names. `lines` is marked `@deprecated` in the code.\n\n- **Change:** `src/api/responses.ts` builds the array once and returns it as both `items` and `lines`.\n- **Other endpoints:** `POST /orders`, `POST /orders/{id}/cancel` and `GET /orders` also return `items`, because they share the same mapper.\n- **Tests:** I updated two assertions in `test/app.test.ts` that pinned the exact response keys.\n\nDropping `lines` needs a deprecation step first. web-storefront has to move to `items`, and then `lines` can be removed. I can add a note about that if you want one.",
